diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,7 +1,83 @@
-# Tauri + Vanilla TS
+# Mabel
 
-This template should help get you started developing with Tauri in vanilla HTML, CSS and Typescript.
+Privacy-first dictation for macOS. Press your hotkey, speak, and the text
+pastes into whatever app has focus. Your audio never leaves your Mac.
 
-## Recommended IDE Setup
+Named after a long-haired Persian who looks judgmental but is, in fact, a
+sweetheart.
 
-- [VS Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/) + [Tauri](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=tauri-apps.tauri-vscode) + [rust-analyzer](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=rust-lang.rust-analyzer)
+## Status
+
+Free tier, internal alpha. macOS Apple Silicon only for now.
+
+## How it works
+
+- Press the configured global hotkey from anywhere on your Mac.
+- Mabel records from your selected microphone.
+- Audio is transcribed locally via a bundled whisper.cpp binary, or via the
+  Groq cloud API if you've supplied your own key in Settings.
+- The transcription pastes into the focused app via the system clipboard,
+  which is then wiped immediately so other apps and clipboard managers don't
+  retain it.
+- Audio is deleted the moment transcription finishes. Only counts and dates
+  are kept locally.
+
+## Build
+
+Requirements: Rust (`brew install rust`), Node 20+, the whisper.cpp binary
+built once (one-time setup below).
+
+```bash
+# One-time: build the whisper sidecar
+git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp.git
+cd whisper.cpp
+cmake -B build
+cmake --build build --config Release -j
+mkdir -p ../mabel/src-tauri/binaries
+cp build/bin/whisper-cli ../mabel/src-tauri/binaries/whisper-cpp-aarch64-apple-darwin
+chmod +x ../mabel/src-tauri/binaries/whisper-cpp-aarch64-apple-darwin
+
+# Dev mode (terminal must stay open)
+cd ../mabel
+npm install
+npm run tauri dev
+
+# Release build
+npm run tauri build
+# Output: src-tauri/target/release/bundle/macos/Mabel.app
+#         src-tauri/target/release/bundle/dmg/Mabel_0.1.0_aarch64.dmg
+```
+
+The release build produces a real .app you can drag to /Applications. First
+launch will show a Gatekeeper warning because the build is unsigned. Right-click
+the app and select Open the first time. Notarization comes later.
+
+## Permissions Mabel asks for
+
+- **Microphone** — to capture your voice.
+- **Accessibility** — to send the paste keystroke into the focused app.
+
+That's it. No location, no contacts, no network access beyond the model
+download and (optionally) your own Groq key.
+
+## Privacy
+
+- 0 audio recordings retained beyond a single transcription.
+- 0 transcripts uploaded.
+- 0 telemetry, analytics, or pings home.
+- Settings live in `~/Library/Application Support/com.mabel.app/`.
+- The Groq API key, if you set one, lives in your macOS Keychain, not on disk.
+- Local stats are counts and dates only. No content. Reset anytime in
+  Settings → Privacy.
+
+## Roadmap
+
+The free tier (this build) gives you unlimited local Whisper transcription
+forever. Pro features (on-device LLM cleanup, app-aware formatting, custom
+vocabulary, voice-to-snippet shortcuts, iCloud settings sync) ship in v2 as
+a paid subscription.
+
+## License
+
+MIT for the app code. Whisper models and the whisper.cpp binary are governed
+by their respective upstream licenses.
